OL,3,GNEWSAFamilies hope Southport Inquiry
OL,4,Awill bring 'meaningful' change
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe families of children injured in the
OL,7,FSouthport attack hope the second phase
OL,8,Fof an inquiry into what happened will
OL,9,Fbring "meaningful" change.
OL,11,FPhase two of the Southport Inquiry
OL,12,Fopens today, with two weeks of
OL,13,Fseminar-style hearings exploring topics
OL,14,Frelated to violence-fixated
OL,15,Findividuals.
OL,17,FAlice da Silva Aguiar, nine, Bebe King,
OL,18,Fsix, and Elsie Dot Stancombe, seven,
OL,19,Fwere killed in the incident, and 23
OL,20,Fother children escaped but suffered
OL,21,Fphysical and psychological harm.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,406,400,260,160,0,100
